=\"4.9\" r=\".95\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/></svg></button\n><span class=\"tipbox\" role=\"tooltip\" id=\"tip-sbnew-about-t\"><span id=\"sbnew-about\">An SIR outbreak in one closed population, the smallest epidemic the filter can fit: infection, recovery, and a tally of infections whose weekly increment, scaled by the ascertainment, is the observed count.</span></span></span></span>\n    </div>\n    \n    <fieldset class=\"sbshipped\" id=\"sbnew-shipped\">\n     <legend>Oracle SIHRS filter</legend>\n     <div class=\"row sb-shiprow\">\n      \n      <span class=\"sbnew-hub\"><label for=\"sbnew-loc\">Location</label>\n       <select id=\"sbnew-loc\" name=\"location\"><option value=\"Alabama\">Alabama</option></select></span>\n      <span class=\"sbnew-hub\"><div class=\"lblrow\"><label for=\"sbnew-date\">Forecast date</label><span class=\"tip\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tipbtn\"\n aria-label=\"About forecast date\" aria-describedby=\"tip-sb-fdate\">?</button\n><span class=\"tipbox\" role=\"tooltip\" id=\"tip-sb-fdate\">The hub vintage archived that day: the data exactly as the forecaster saw it then.</span></span></div>\n       <select id=\"sbnew-date\" name=\"forecast_date\"><option value=\"2025-01-11\">2025-01-11</option></select></span>\n      \n      \n      <span><div class=\"lblrow\"><label for=\"sbnew-season\">Season start</label><span class=\"tip\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tipbtn\"\n aria-label=\"About season start\" aria-describedby=\"tip-sb-season\">?</button\n><span class=\"tipbox\" role=\"tooltip\" id=\"tip-sb-season\">Optional. t = 0 and the seasonal phase count from it; blank takes August 1, as production does.</span></span></div>\n       <input id=\"sbnew-season\" name=\"season_start\" type=\"date\" value=\"\"></span>\n     </div>\n    </fieldset>\n    <div class=\"row\"><button class=\"gold\">Create</button></div>\n   </form>\n  </div>\n  \n  <details class=\"card sbhow\" open><summary><h2>How the Sandbox works</h2></summary>\n   \n\n<ol class=\"uk-stepper uk-stepper--vertical\" aria-label=\"How the Sandbox works\">\n<li class=\"uk-step uk-step--todo\"><span class=\"uk-step-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1</span><span class=\"uk-step-body\"><span class=\"uk-step-label\">Start a model</span><span class=\"uk-step-meta\">The SIR example is the place to learn; a template adapts to a new pathogen.</span></span></li>\n<li class=\"uk-step uk-step--todo\"><span class=\"uk-step-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2</span><span class=\"uk-step-body\"><span class=\"uk-step-label\">Edit its three files</span><span class=\"uk-step-meta\">model.bngl: the model (names ending __FREE are fitted); data.exp: the weekly counts; priors.conf: each fitted value&#39;s range. Load data or Simulate data on the data.exp tab.</span></span></li>\n<li class=\"uk-step uk-step--todo\"><span class=\"uk-step-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3</span><span class=\"uk-step-body\"><span class=\"uk-step-label\">Check</span><span class=\"uk-step-meta\">What would stop a run, and the model beside the data, without fitting.</span></span></li>\n<li class=\"uk-step uk-step--todo\"><span class=\"uk-step-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4</span><span class=\"uk-step-body\"><span class=\"uk-step-label\">Save and run</span><span class=\"uk-step-meta\">The full fit (10,000 particles) gives the estimates; with a quick check (200) the ranges are rough.</span></span></li>\n<li class=\"uk-step uk-step--todo\"><span class=\"uk-step-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5</span><span class=\"uk-step-body\"><span class=\"uk-step-label\">Read the result</span><span class=\"uk-step-meta\">The effective sample size (ESS) grades the sampling; the band meets the data; each fitted value with its 5 to 95% range.</span></span></li>\n<li class=\"uk-step uk-step--todo\"><span class=\"uk-step-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6</span><span class=\"uk-step-body\"><span class=\"uk-step-label\">Try a change</span><span class=\"uk-step-meta\">Edit and run again, or Duplicate it; Compare with lists what changed.</span></span></li></ol>\n  </details>\n </div>\n <div>\n  <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"uk-heading\"><h2 id=\"h-sb-models\">Your models</h2></div>\n   <div class=\"uk-empty\" id=\"sb-nomodels\"><svg class=\"uk-icon uk-empty-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"1em\" height=\"1em\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><path d=\"M1.9 4.3c0-.6.4-1 1-1h3.3l1.5 1.7h5.4c.6 0 1 .4 1 1v6.8c0 .6-.4 1-1 1H2.9c-.6 0-1-.4-1-1Z\"/></svg><p class=\"uk-empty-title\">No models yet</p></div>\n  </div>\n  \n  <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"uk-heading\"><h2 id=\"h-sb-exp\">Experiments</h2></div>\n   \n   <form method=\"post\" action=\"/sandbox/experiments\">\n    <div class=\"sb-shiprow\">\n     <span><label for=\"sbexp-model\">Model</label>\n      <select id=\"sbexp-model\" name=\"model\">\n       <optgroup label=\"Shipped\"><option value=\"sihrs\" data-oracle=\"1\">sihrs \u00b7 the Oracle SIHRS, as shipped</option><option value=\"sihrs-2strain\" data-oracle=\"0\">sihrs-2strain \u00b7 influenza A and B (research)</option><option value=\"sihrs-natg\" data-oracle=\"0\">sihrs-natg \u00b7 with a national-growth factor (research)</option></optgroup>\n       <optgroup label=\"Registered\"><option value=\"beta@1\" data-oracle=\"0\" selected>beta@1 \u00b7 5edca88e</option></optgroup>\n      </select></span>\n     <span><label for=\"sbexp-season\">Season</label>\n      <select id=\"sbexp-season\" name=\"season\"><option value=\"2024-25\" selected>2024-25 \u00b7 shipped replay here</option></select></span>\n     <span><label for=\"sbexp-size\">Size</label>\n      <select id=\"sbexp-size\" name=\"size\">\n       <option value=\"smoke\" selected>smoke: 2 locations, 2 weeks (about 1 to 4 min)</option>\n       <option value=\"pilot\">pilot: 10 locations, every other week (about 14 to 56 min)</option>\n       <option value=\"full\">full: every location and week